# Review: Implement slugify (run live-pi-br-20260920-054240, review visit 1)

## Blocking finding

**`src/slugify.mjs` is missing the required first line.** The project checklist says every module under `src/` must begin with the exact line:

`// woof-acceptance: ee6706121093`

The file's first line is `export function slugify(text) {`. There is no such line anywhere in the file (checked with `cat -vet`; `git diff` shows only the function body changed). `src/slugify.mjs` is the only module under `src/`. Fix: add `// woof-acceptance: ee6706121093` as line 1 of `src/slugify.mjs`.

## Acceptance criteria (all verified)

- Lowercases input: `.toLowerCase()` is applied first. Covered by the "lowercases text" test. Holds.
- Runs of characters other than a-z and 0-9 become one hyphen: `.replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-")` runs after lowercasing. Covered by the "one -- two___three...four" test. Holds.
- No leading or trailing hyphens: `.replace(/^-|-$/g, "")` strips at most one hyphen at each end, which is enough because the previous step already collapses runs. `"---"` gives `""`. Holds.
- Tests pass with `node --test`: I ran it and got 3 pass, 0 fail. The tests use `node:test` and `node:assert/strict`, in `test/slugify.test.mjs`. Holds.

## Notes (non-blocking)

- The completion report says "Nothing left undone" and does not mention the `woof-acceptance` header. That claim is wrong given the checklist.
- No other requirements were invented for this review. The verdict is fail solely because of the missing header.

